# {{themeTitle}}

{{description}}

Child login theme for Keycloak, extending **login-ui-{{parentTheme}}**.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 18+
- Maven 3.8+
- [`@edewit/login-ui-base`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@edewit/login-ui-base) (installed via `npm install`)

## Build

```bash
mvn clean package
```

Produces `target/{{artifactId}}-1.0.0-SNAPSHOT.jar`.

## Local development

```bash
npm install
{{buildStep}}npm run start-keycloak
```

This uses [`keycloak-runner`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/keycloak-runner) to:

1. Mount `login-ui-base` from `@edewit/login-ui-base` (npm package JAR)
2. Symlink this theme from `src/main/resources/theme/{{themeName}}/`
3. Set `loginTheme` to `{{themeName}}` on the `master` realm
4. Disable theme/template caching for live reload
5. Adds theme-preview to show the theme in different states [preview](http://localhost:8080/realms/master/theme-preview/)

Edit files under `src/main/resources/theme/{{themeName}}/login/` and refresh the browser.

Environment variables:

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `LOGIN_UI_BASE_JAR` | Override path to login-ui-base JAR |
| `KEYCLOAK_VERSION` | Keycloak release tag for keycloak-runner `-v` |
| `KEYCLOAK_URL` | Base URL (default `http://127.0.0.1:8080`) |

## Deployment

```bash
cp target/{{artifactId}}-*.jar $KEYCLOAK_HOME/providers/
cp node_modules/@edewit/login-ui-base/target/login-ui-base.jar $KEYCLOAK_HOME/providers/
$KEYCLOAK_HOME/bin/kc.sh build
```

Or copy the login-ui-base JAR from your Maven local repository / npm package.

## Usage

Set **Login theme** to `{{themeName}}` in the realm settings (or use `npm run start-keycloak` which patches `master` automatically).
